In India, thousands of women have been taking to the streets calling for better protection of female students, following the suspected gang rape of a 17-year-old girl. The alleged incident in an upscale neighbourhood of New Delhi prompted authorities to beef up protective measures, but the women say limiting their access to public spaces is not the answer. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13c9f100-be66-11f1-9fce-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/Students-New-Delhi-000-C9T27KN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13c9f100-be66-11f1-9fce-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/Students-New-Delhi-000-C9T27KN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe07b03a-be4e-11f1-9011-fb1f4723fc15</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 14:57:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Thailand floods: At least 8 die, thousands move to shelters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-thailand-floods-at-least-8-die-thousands-move-to-shelters</link><description>
Rain eased in Thailand ’s capital on Sunday, but flooding persisted in several low-lying areas, with thousands forced to move into temporary shelters. At least eight people were reported killed in the past 10 days nationwide.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b0a755e-bb2c-11f1-a50d-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/minithai.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b0a755e-bb2c-11f1-a50d-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/minithai.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">807ddc90-bb2c-11f1-a88c-f3299f89d967</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:20:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Thousands evacuated amid Bangkok floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-evacuated-amid-bangkok-floods</link><description>
Rain is easing in Thailand’s capital, but flooding continues in several low-lying areas. Thousands of people have been forced into temporary shelters after the government declared Bangkok a disaster zone on Saturday. At least eight people have died over the past 10 days as heavy rains caused widespread disruption. Juliette Brown reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27f9a0a2-ba7a-11f1-89cb-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260927-150645-150805-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27f9a0a2-ba7a-11f1-89cb-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260927-150645-150805-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2d0c2ee8-ba7a-11f1-a68c-3f06bb9ef66b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:59:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>A month after, thousands are still missing and families face a long recovery</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/a-month-after-thousands-are-still-missing-and-families-face-a-long-recovery</link><description>
 A month after Nepal’s floods, thousands are still missing and families face a long recovery.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d8e1e50-b983-11f1-9be0-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260926-081816-082022-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d8e1e50-b983-11f1-9be0-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260926-081816-082022-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">835448fa-b983-11f1-a6f5-db4c14db2b04</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:40:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Bangkok declares flood disaster after massive 48-hour downpour</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260926-bangkok-declares-flood-disaster-after-massive-48h-downpour</link><description>
Thailand’s capital Bangkok declared a flood disaster on Saturday after more than 300 millimetres of rain in less than 48 hours, leaving canals overflowing and streets submerged. “It’s like at my waist level now,” a local said. The governor has urged people not to panic, saying the situation is stabilising. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59f5dfba-b964-11f1-a3bf-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/64c8a3ae733e432164095f1d6ce0dec42577a2b2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59f5dfba-b964-11f1-a3bf-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/64c8a3ae733e432164095f1d6ce0dec42577a2b2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5accd74a-b964-11f1-8990-fbfaa5866bba</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:40:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59f5dfba-b964-11f1-a3bf-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/64c8a3ae733e432164095f1d6ce0dec42577a2b2.jpg">© Lillian Suwanrumpha, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Fatalities on Indian roads: One death reported every three minutes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260925-fatalities-on-indian-roads-one-death-reported-every-three-minutes</link><description>
India has the second-largest road network in the world, spanning over 6 million kilometres. But these roads are silent killers, with one death reported every three minutes. Every day, headlines are filled with horror stories: drunk drivers mowing people down, school buses hit by speeding trucks killing children, buses with dozens of passengers plunging into gorges.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd861ccc-b82a-11f1-ab73-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-INDIA-ROAD-SAFETY-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd861ccc-b82a-11f1-ab73-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-INDIA-ROAD-SAFETY-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c6ae98c-b82b-11f1-8dd9-1bd6ea2dfd4d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:33:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Navodita KUMARI</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>Journalism and resistance under Taliban rule</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260925-journalism-and-resistance-under-taliban-rule</link><description>
In this edition, we focus on Afghanistan, which recently marked the fifth anniversary of the Taliban's return to power. Since then, the exclusion of women and girls has become normalised, with the government systematically dismantling the rights of more than half the country's population.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f937a684-b8c5-11f1-9764-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/vanishing-girl-kabul-web-photo.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f937a684-b8c5-11f1-9764-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/vanishing-girl-kabul-web-photo.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65703b5e-b8c6-11f1-94d9-1d5ad55c08cb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:21:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Nepal’s catastrophic floods were ‘warning to the world', PM Shah tells UN</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260925-nepal-floods-warning-world-pm-shah-un</link><description>
Nepal’s Prime Minister Balendra Shah said on Thursday that last month’s catastrophic floods were a “warning to the world” of growing climate risks in the Himalayas. He said warming was melting glaciers and permafrost and urged international support to help Nepal adapt to threats it could not face alone.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/076076f0-b87b-11f1-98d9-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268010715411.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/076076f0-b87b-11f1-98d9-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268010715411.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c2cea702-b878-11f1-9b77-032513e246ea</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:42:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/076076f0-b87b-11f1-98d9-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268010715411.jpg">© Frank Franklin II, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61aec282-b827-11f1-9e10-a18ad05a0c45/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-150401-151641-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61aec282-b827-11f1-9e10-a18ad05a0c45/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-150401-151641-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">67883378-b827-11f1-884b-af4a0164a4c2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:01:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Taiwan: Home of semiconductor giants at the centre of AI race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race</link><description>
The topic of artificial intelligence looms large as Chinese President Xi Jinping begins his highly anticipated state visit to Washington. The fate of Taiwan – coveted by its larger neighbour, China – will also be on the table. It's the global leader in superconductor research and development. These powerful chips can be found in smartphones, computers, and above all in AI development. Our France 2 colleagues take a rare look inside one of Taiwan's state-of-the-art laboratories. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e389a8a-b755-11f1-9ee0-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-TAIWAN-SEMICONS-BAIN-Lauren-transfer.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e389a8a-b755-11f1-9ee0-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-TAIWAN-SEMICONS-BAIN-Lauren-transfer.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">833f3c38-b755-11f1-bc38-954786cdc9c7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:17:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 2</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Pakistan launches air strikes in Afghanistan, killing civilians, Taliban says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260924-pakistan-launches-air-strikes-in-afghanistan-killing-civilians-taliban-says</link><description>
Pakistan launched air strikes Thursday on 10 sites in Afghanistan in what Islamabad said was a retaliation for a drone attack by Afghanistan's Taliban forces on a border post. A Taliban government spokesman denied the allegation and said Pakistan's latest strikes killed four civilians in Afghanistan's southern and eastern provinces.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc68d050-b7ef-11f1-8d15-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C98C8ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc68d050-b7ef-11f1-8d15-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C98C8ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63679d7e-b7f0-11f1-a287-4f7b4376ab75</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:53:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc68d050-b7ef-11f1-8d15-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C98C8ZQ.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
